Subject: Memoize the (shape, key) to index mapping for element loads

What this does
  Remembers the slot an element load resolved to, keyed on the receiver's shape
  and the key.

Why we need it
  Repeated loads on the same layout repeat the walk that found the slot.

What it adds
  The memo holds a counted reference to the shape, so it cannot outlive the layout
  it describes, and it is consulted only for a receiver whose shape still matches.
  A miss, a shape change, a proxy and any receiver the fast element path already
  declines take the existing path. No opcode is added or retired and BC_VERSION is
  unchanged.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -458,6 +458,17 @@
